  "description": "Production route inventory (CONTROL-DURABILITY). Every /api route the production app registers, grouped by how it behaves in production. Checked by src/tests/productionRouteInventory.test.ts. A durableReplacement names the route cutover key (src/server/routeCutover.ts) of the durable router that covers the same work; it is not mounted until its proposals are owner-approved.",
  "kinds": {
    "VOLATILE_REFUSED": "Backed by process-local (in-memory) state. Production refuses with the group's code, after authentication and scope checks, so nothing a restart or a second instance would lose is served or acknowledged. Needs a durable adapter.",
    "DURABLE_GATED": "A durable adapter exists but is off until its proposal is approved and applied and the switch is set; until then production refuses with the group's code.",
    "PROVIDER_REFUSED": "Depends on an external provider that is not commissioned; production refuses with the group's code.",
    "RETIRED": "Local password and identity routes retired in production in favour of the Supabase session bridge (410).",
    "DURABLE": "Reads or writes PostgreSQL or the durable session store through the server role. With the synthetic store in this test it reports its provider unavailable or answers from the synthetic session rows.",
    "STATELESS": "Computes only from the request or from a static reference catalog; it reads and records no case state.",
    "DIAGNOSTIC": "Liveness, readiness and administrator-only diagnostics; no client records."
  },
